<title>JAPAN: Mexico launches 70 bln yen 6-yr samurai bonds.</title>
<headline>Mexico launches 70 bln yen 6-yr samurai bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico on Wednesday launched 70 billion yen worth of samurai bonds due September 30, 2002, lead-manager Daiwa Securities Co Ltd said.</p>
<p>The bonds carry a coupon rate of 5.0 percent and were priced at par, Daiwa said.  </p>
<p>The breakdown of the terms is as follows.</p>
<p> AMT 70 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON  5.0 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY Sept 30 2002</p>
<p> TYPE  samurai</p>
<p> ISS PRICE  par</p>
<p> PAY DATE Sept 30 1996</p>
<p> SIGN DATE	    Sept 11</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	   from Sept 13 to Sept 26</p>
<p> INTEREST PAYMENT   end March and end Sept yearly</p>
<p> LAST RATING	  BB (S&amp;P)</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER	 Daiwa Securities Co Ltd</p>
</text>
